WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:02.602
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.070
This is "Late Night."
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.238
And now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:08.073
Former President Trump's
attorney Joe Tacopina

00:00:08.073 --> 00:00:10.143
said in a new interview
that it was a, quote,

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:13.145
"relief" to see the final
charges against Trump.

00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:17.450
Alright, you know it's bad
when 34 felonies is a relief.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:22.055
Phew, really dodged
a bullet there.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.756
After attending a rally
in Manhattan

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:25.758
in support of former
President Trump on Tuesday,

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:27.626
Georgia Congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:00:27.626 --> 00:00:29.595
criticized New York
during an interview

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:31.263
with Fox News host
Tucker Carlson

00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:33.466
and said, "I think
it's a very terrible place."

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.935
But the joke's on you,
Marjorie,

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:39.472
because once you think that,
you're officially a New Yorker.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:42.008
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.510
After he was arraigned
on Tuesday in Manhattan,

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:45.711
Former President Trump
reportedly

00:00:45.711 --> 00:00:48.014
sat on the patio at Mar-a-Lago

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:51.083
and used his iPad to play music
over the club's speakers,

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:54.053
including "Macho Man"
by the Village People.

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:56.356
"Hey man, you can't play
that here anymore,"

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.525
said the governor
of Florida.

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:00.994
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:03.896
According to a new report
from the EPA,

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:05.965
there are more than
1 million lead pipes

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.399
still in use in Florida.

00:01:07.399 --> 00:01:10.069
And there are actually
more than that in New Jersey,

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:13.139
but they don't want
to have to use them.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.374
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:18.577
You know what I mean?

00:01:18.577 --> 00:01:20.713
Lamborghini this week
unveiled its first

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.481
plug-in hybrid supercar.

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:25.284
Now you can help save
the planet for your children

00:01:25.284 --> 00:01:27.520
from all three
of your marriages.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.256
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.925
A government official
in Singapore

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:34.160
was recently sentenced
to two years in jail

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.561
after he allegedly
sold more than

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:38.330
600 stolen printer cartridges
online.

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:42.502
No word on what happened to the
trillions of dollars he made.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.006
I'm from the generation
where we had to buy

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.007
our own printer cartridge.

00:01:49.007 --> 00:01:50.743
They get you on the cyan?

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.145
Is that the one
they get you on, Baze?

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.780
Yeah.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.484
According to a new survey,

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:00.787
an estimated
44 million American adults

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.688
are experiencing
significant loneliness,

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:04.891
which explains why they were
willing to take a survey.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:10.062
"No, it's not.
It's not a bad time at all."

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:12.264
A person walking
on a beach in Florida

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:15.134
recently found a 30-pound
bale of marijuana,

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.002
and they admittedly
did the right thing

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:20.673
and reported the 25-pound
bale of marijuana.

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:25.778
According to a new study,

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:28.381
poor sleep can increase
the risk of a stroke.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:31.084
But on the plus side,
you got to hear this joke.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:33.253
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.926
Two former prison guards
in Oklahoma

00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:43.062
were recently sentenced
to probation for allegedly

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:47.066
forcing inmates to listen to the
song "Baby Shark" as punishment.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:51.070
And it's worse than you think,
because they played it twice.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.474
That's right, two former
prison guards in Oklahoma

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.643
were recently sentenced
to probation for allegedly

00:02:57.643 --> 00:03:01.214
forcing inmates to listen
to the song "Baby Shark."

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.549
Meanwhile, a local charity
in New York

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:07.153
remains unpunished.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:10.056
And that was a monologue,
everybody.

